<title>SINGAPORE: Sri Lanka awards naphtha sale tender to Glencore.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka awards naphtha sale tender to Glencore.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's state-owned Ceylon Petroleum Corp has awarded its January naphtha sell tender for 25,000 tonnes to Swiss trader Glencore at 73 cents below Singapore spot quotes, a CPC official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender for light naphtha lifting January 20-21 was awarded on a free-on-board Colombo basis, the official said.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold 125,000-barrels lifting November 28-29 at 62 cents below Singapore quotes to Japanese trader Marubeni.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
